2026-09-30 05:12 Research: Langfuse usage_details keys are mutually exclusive buckets (docs token-and-cost-tracking#usage-details-contract): input excludes input_*; total = sum. Flat usageDetails and langfuse.observation.usage_details are stored unchanged, so Knarr must send exclusive counts. Langfuse's own normalizer (OtelIngestionProcessor, AI SDK path) names cache reads input_cached_tokens and writes input_cache_creation (+ _5m/_1h tiers); default-model-prices.json prices those keys for every OpenAI/Anthropic/Gemini model that has any cache price. So: NOT 'fold cache into input AND send details' (that double-counts cost) -- input = uncached input, cache as input_cached_tokens / input_cache_creation. Legacy v2 usage keeps inclusive input; v3 overlays usageDetails keys over usage (IngestionService), so v3 sees exclusive. Paths: routed Response/Stream usage = Langertha::Usage from_hash with raw provider hash (0.503 has no cache accessors, dev core does); PassthroughUsage keeps provider hash verbatim incl. cache keys (merge over message_start).

